Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Carveout bundles none of the software below. Each is installed from its own
upstream by the environment setup or bundled into the browser front-end at build
time, and remains governed by its own licence. This file is a summary for convenience, not a
substitute for those licences.

SAM 3 / SAM 3.1  —  Meta Platforms, Inc.
    https://github.com/facebookresearch/sam3
    Licence: SAM License (custom, non-OSI). Model weights are distributed under
    gated access on Hugging Face (facebook/sam3, facebook/sam3.1) and require
    the user to request access and accept Meta's terms directly.
    Carveout redistributes neither the code nor the weights: the `sam3` package
    is installed from Meta's repository and the checkpoints are downloaded by the
    user. The segmentation stage is unusable without them.

    Carveout integrates SAM 3 at ARM'S LENGTH — as a user-installed external
    package called through its published API, not as a bundled, derived or
    combined work distributed by this project. Carveout's own code is
    GPL-3.0-or-later; SAM 3 remains governed by Meta's SAM License, which each
    user accepts directly, INCLUDING ITS FIELD-OF-USE RESTRICTIONS. Those
    restrictions bind your use of SAM 3; they do not attach to Carveout's code.

gsplat  —  nerfstudio project
    https://github.com/nerfstudio-project/gsplat
    Licence: Apache License 2.0.
    Installed as a Python dependency; used to rasterise views and to attribute
    rendered masks back to individual Gaussians.

three.js  —  three.js authors
    https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js
    Licence: MIT.
    Bundled into the browser front-end at build time (declared in
    webui/package.json).

SparkJS  —  https://github.com/sparkjs-dev/spark  (https://sparkjs.dev/)
    Licence: MIT.
    Gaussian-splat rendering in the browser front-end; bundled at build time.

Qwen3.8-27B and Qwen3-VL-8B  —  Alibaba Cloud / Qwen team
    https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B
    https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct
    Licence: Apache License 2.0. Ungated: no access request and no terms to
    accept, unlike the SAM 3 checkpoints above.
    Carveout redistributes neither the weights nor any Qwen code. The weights
    are downloaded by the user (README step 7) into models/, which is not in
    this repository, and are loaded through the `transformers` library. One
    of the two, chosen per scene, serves the three OPTIONAL vision-model uses
    — the second opinion on a measured length at the volume gate, the
    vocabulary proposal, and label verification — each of which refuses with
    the download command when the weights are absent. The rest of the
    pipeline never loads them.

React, Vite, Tailwind CSS, and the other build-time dependencies of the browser
front-end are declared in webui/package.json with their own licences; they are
build and runtime dependencies of that bundle only.

PyTorch, torchvision, NumPy, Pillow, matplotlib, plyfile, PyYAML, huggingface_hub
and the remaining Python dependencies are declared in environment.yml and
pyproject.toml, and are installed from PyPI under their own licences.

Fonts: the browser front-end bundles Inter, IBM Plex Mono and Figtree via
@fontsource (SIL Open Font License 1.1) at build time and fetches no font at
runtime.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Services
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

None. Carveout makes no network calls at run time and sends no data off the
machine. The optional vision-model stages run a local model, downloaded by the
user alongside the SAM 3 checkpoints (see README). There is no API key.
